From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 20:28:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: aw88166: support changing sample rate and bit
 width

The aw88166 driver only worked with the stream configuration baked
into the loaded acf profile due to the lack of a proper PLL
initialization sequence. Fix by selecting all the necessary PLL
settings based on what was passed to us by the hw_params/set_fmt ops.
This replaces the strange downstream routine that tries two divider
modes in sequence.

Adapted for aw88166 from Val Packett's aw88261 series:
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260529200507.…-val@packett.cool/
Register layout verified against Awinic's downstream
---
